# Local tooling, not project deliverable: skills, workflows and the constitution live here
# purely for portability (copy the folder to move the whole line to another repo), not for
# git to sync them across clones or worktrees. Nothing in CI or scripts/gate.sh reads .claude
# -- the harness and dependency gates that matter live in tracked files outside it. A spec is
# published by `/specify {github:true}`, which force-adds just that one feature directory.
.claude/
AGENTS.md
.codegraph
# local analysis scratch (not committed)
.scratch/
evaluation/results/.judge_cache/
.sonar
# CLAUDE.md is the agent contract (container-not-host, no-silent-fallback, the
# gate layout). Ignoring it is how this repo ended up with a CLAUDE.md
# describing an entirely different project -- so it is tracked, and the rule that
# ignored it anyway five lines below this comment is gone.

graphify-out
prototypes
.scratch*
# Candidate ontologies under evaluation — not part of the shipped bundle.
# Scoped to `candidates/` on purpose: hatchling drops VCS-ignored files from the
# wheel, so a broader `assets/` rule would silently unship cco/cco.json, which
# `GraphKnowsSettings.ontology_source` defaults to.
# The path moved with the package (frames/ + ontology/ -> symbolic/). A stale
# path here fails SILENTLY: the files simply stop being ignored, get swept in
# by `git add processrecall/`, and the large-file hook then rejects the whole
# commit on a 4.6 MB .owl that was never meant to be committed.
processrecall/symbolic/ontology/assets/cco-extensions/candidates/
# machine-written run reports; the rules beside runs/ stay tracked
docs/agents/runs/
docs\adr
.claude\settings.local.json
